# Git must not touch these files. The corpus records CHARACTER OFFSETS into
# every source file, and Σ(f) joins its fact tables to those offsets. A CRLF
# conversion on checkout shifts each one by the number of preceding lines, so
# a round trip through Windows silently moves every function by a different
# amount and the join quietly attaches facts to the wrong declaration.
#
# This is not hypothetical: the same tree hashed differently on Linux after a
# push from Windows, which is what sent `corpus` permanently STALE.
* -text

*.sh text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
